Looking at Figure 3b, SELECT has ~800 standard regret vs SAT-UCB ~500 and SAT-UCB+ ~600. However, the Convex ALG (the oracle) has ~1000. SELECT does beat the oracle it uses. The baselines SAT-UCB and SAT-UCB+ are "heuristics" without regret guarantees in this setting. The paper's claim of "good enough distribution" is vague but not an outright lie. However, the conclusion claims "excellent performances... in both the realizable and the non-realizable cases" which overstates the concave non-realizable results.

